<section class="answer-block" id="answer" aria-label="Direct answer">
  <div class="wrap">
    <h2 class="answer-q">Where do the numbers on khadijazaman.com come from?</h2>
    <p class="answer-a">Every figure on khadijazaman.com is measured in GA4 or Google Search Console by Khadija Zaman, reported by a named third party, or cited from a published document, and this page lists the property, window, source and last-verified date for each one. Figures that cannot be checked from outside, such as the 22× LLM referral growth for a confidential client with no published baseline, are marked as headline-only rather than confirmed.</p>
  </div>
</section>

<section aria-label="Provenance table" style="padding-top:0;">
  <div class="wrap">
    {%- set confirmed = 0 %}{%- for f in provenance %}{% if f.status == "confirmed" %}{% set confirmed = confirmed + 1 %}{% endif %}{% endfor %}
    <p class="num-note reveal">{{ provenance.length }} figures. {{ confirmed }} confirmed, meaning a named source and a verified date. The rest say what is missing. Machine-readable copy: <a href="/provenance.json">/provenance.json</a>. Method key: <strong>measured</strong> by Khadija from the named property; <strong>reported</strong> by a third party; <strong>cited</strong> from a published document.</p>
    <div class="cs-table-wrap">
      <table class="cs-table prov-table">
        <thead><tr><th>Figure</th><th>Claim</th><th>Property · window</th><th>Source · method</th><th>Evidence</th><th>Verified</th><th>Status</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
        {%- for f in provenance %}
          <tr id="{{ f.id }}">
            <td class="prov-fig" data-l="Figure">{% if f.figure %}{{ f.figure }}{% else %}<span class="prov-null">null</span>{% endif %}</td>
            <td data-l="Claim">{{ f.claim }}{% if f.note %}<div class="prov-note">{{ f.note }}</div>{% endif %}</td>
            <td data-l="Property · window">{{ f.property }}<div class="prov-note">{{ f.window }}</div></td>
            <td data-l="Source · method">{{ f.source }}<div class="prov-note">{{ f.method }}</div></td>
            <td data-l="Evidence">{% if f.evidence %}<a href="{{ f.evidence }}"{% if f.evidence.indexOf(site.url) != 0 %} target="_blank" rel="noopener"{% endif %}>{{ f.evidenceLabel }}</a>{% else %}<span class="prov-null">none public</span>{% endif %}</td>
            <td data-l="Verified">{% if f.verified %}{{ f.verified }}{% else %}<span class="prov-null">null</span>{% endif %}</td>
            <td data-l="Status"><span class="prov-status{% if f.status == 'confirmed' %} ok{% endif %}">{{ f.status }}</span></td>
          </tr>
        {%- endfor %}
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
    <p class="press-scope">Rows with a null verified date were written down from the source at the time and have not been re-checked since; they will be confirmed or corrected as Khadija re-opens each property. The 680K → 3.78M impressions figure is flagged because the on-site screenshot shows a three-month comparison while the label says 12 months.</p>
  </div>
</section>
